.TH MS 1 "December 2025" "ms 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ms \- Python-based 'ls' replacement with tree view
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ms
[\fI\-a\fR] [\fI\-l\fR] [\fI\-H\fR] [\fI\-t\fR] [\fIpath\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ms
is a Python-based replacement for the Unix
.B ls
command, with additional features like tree view, colorized output, and human-readable file sizes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Show hidden files (those starting with a dot).
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-long
Use a long listing format, showing permissions, size, and modification time.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-human
Display file sizes in human-readable format (e.g., KB, MB, GB).
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-tree
Display directories and files in a tree-like structure.
.TP
.B path
The directory to list. Defaults to the current directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ms
List files in the current directory.
.TP
.B ms \-l
List files in long format.
.TP
.B ms \-a
List all files, including hidden ones.
.TP
.B ms \-t
List files and directories in a tree view.
.TP
.B ms \-lH
List files in long format with human-readable sizes.
.TP
.B ms /path/to/dir
List files in the specified directory.
